  "summary": "DESIGN-20261102-Q5MU Completion-stage tech-debt closure, folded into the still-unconsumed 3.2.0 release rather than a new version bump (developer's call -- v3.2.0.zip exists but nothing has pulled it yet): (1) fixed a real bug in docs.mjs's assign() that crashed build()/reindex() on any doc move/rename when the frontmatter id stayed the same (TD-10, RF-048), with a new regression test; (2) fixed the canonical design/01-context-gathering.md template's own root cause for a duplicated-rendering bug -- {{DESIGN_CONTEXT_STEP}} was used twice but its value is the full body of Step 3 (TD-3), plus an INTENT.md note warning against reusing it; (3) defined a concrete, verified mechanical staleness check for the graph-query wiring and pointed all 6 canonical wiring points at it instead of leaving \"stale\" undefined (TD-5); (4) wired dev/references/03-plan.md Step 1 to the same query-first graph pattern as every other read-path wiring point (TD-11). Package version stays 3.2.0.",
